# Coach Transparency Guide

> **Role:** Scrum Master / Agile Coach  
> **Framework:** SAFe 6.0 (Scaled Agile Framework)  
> **Objective:** Maximize team alignment, transparency, and relentless improvement by making all SAFe 6.0 artifacts, metrics, and goals constantly visible to the team.

---

## Core Principle: "Radiate Information"

In a SAFe transformation, hidden information creates confusion, friction, and missed commitments. As a Scrum Master, your job is to build **Information Radiators**—visual dashboards and physical/digital spaces where the team sees goals, blockers, metrics, and commitments without having to search for them.

---

## Comprehensive SAFe 6.0 Visibility Matrix

| Category | SAFe 6.0 Artifact / Element | What it Contains & Why it Matters | Where it Must Be Displayed (100% Visibility) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Iteration Level** *(Short-Term)* | **Iteration Goals (Sprint Goals)** | • 1 to 3 business-focused objectives for the current iteration.<br>• Aligns the team on value rather than individual user stories. | • **Jira Board Header:** Custom banner or pinned issue at the top.<br>• **Daily Sync Board:** Top-left banner on digital or physical board.<br>• **Slack/Teams Channel:** Pinned message in team chat. |
| | **Iteration Backlog & WIP** | • All Committed User Stories, Enablers, Bugs, and Spikes.<br>• Real-time progress (`To Do` $\rightarrow$ `In Progress` $\rightarrow$ `Review` $\rightarrow$ `Done`). | • **Active Sprint Board:** Real-time digital board (Jira/Azure DevOps).<br>• **WIP Limits Display:** Explicit numbers above `In Progress` and `Review` columns. |
| | **Definition of Done (DoD) & Definition of Ready (DoR)** | • Clear quality gates for acceptance (e.g., unit tests passed, code review complete, data quality validated). | • **Jira Board Sidebar / Header link**.<br>• **Confluence / Wiki Team Page** (quick reference widget).<br>• Physical poster near the team area (if co-located). |
| **PI Level** *(Program Increment)* | **Team PI Objectives** | • Summary of business and technical goals for the full 8–12 week PI.<br>• Differentiates **Committed Objectives** vs. **Uncommitted Objectives**. | • **Program Room / ART Board:** Dedicated widget or panel.<br>• **Team Dashboard:** Top widget on the primary dashboard.<br>• **Confluence Home Page:** Pinned at the top of the PI space. |
